Summary:
During today’s session, the focus shifted towards refining the existing Developer Portfolio Evaluator project by identifying and fixing bugs encountered in the previous implementation. We revisited the frontend and backend integration to ensure stable communication and resolved issues related to API errors, incorrect request handling, and data inconsistencies. Additional debugging techniques such as logging and step-by-step validation were used to trace and eliminate errors. Minor improvements were also made to enhance input handling and ensure smoother user interaction. The application was re-tested with multiple GitHub usernames to verify consistent performance.

Outcomes:
By the end of the session, the application became more stable and reliable, with major bugs successfully resolved. The API responses were handled more effectively, resulting in accurate and consistent output across different test cases. Improved error handling ensured better feedback for invalid inputs and edge cases. The debugging process strengthened understanding of request flow, backend validation, and frontend-backend synchronization. Overall, the project quality was enhanced, making it more robust and closer to a production-ready application.
